        "Kubernetes pod resource limits should be configured in the deployment manifest. Set resources.requests.memory to the minimum memory the container needs, and resources.limits.memory to the maximum. If a container exceeds its memory limit, it will be terminated and restarted by the kubelet.",
        "The message queue uses a publish-subscribe pattern with guaranteed at-least-once delivery. Consumers must acknowledge messages after processing. Unacknowledged messages are redelivered after a configurable timeout (default: 30 seconds). Duplicate detection is the consumer's responsibility.",
        "To enable TLS 1.3 on the web server, update the ssl_protocols directive in the nginx.conf file to include TLSv1.3. Generate a new certificate using the ECDSA algorithm with a P-256 curve for optimal performance. Restart the nginx service after updating the configuration.",
        "The caching layer uses Redis with a default TTL of 3600 seconds (1 hour). Cache invalidation follows a write-through strategy: when data is updated in the primary database, the corresponding cache entry is immediately deleted. The next read request populates the cache with fresh data.",
        "Error handling in the SDK follows a hierarchy of exception classes. NetworkError is thrown for connectivity issues, AuthenticationError for invalid credentials, ValidationError for malformed requests, and ServerError for 5xx responses. All exceptions extend the base SdkError class.",
